  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `docs/plan/expanding-frontiers-2026-08-28/` — the complete, auditable output of one governed subject-DAG run answering: **which three ideas should be entered into Expanding Frontiers (expandingfrontiers.org) programs, and which single one is most likely to win a grant or award?**\n\n**How the tooling behaved.** `hive-mind autopilot run` on this repository fails closed with `PLAN_GENERATION_REQUIRED`, correctly refusing to reuse the installed controller's plan for a new subject. It returns a host-neutral contract whose declared `execution_owner` is `active_host_sandbox`, so a DAG was generated for this subject and executed by the host. The generated plan validates against the repository's own authoring standard (`dag-lint --strict`: **0 error, 0 warning, 0 info**) and compiles into **8 dispatch rounds**, each of which was then executed.\n\n**Result — verdict `ADAPT`:**\n\n| | Idea | Weighted |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🥇 | Corrosion evidence for coastal launch and energy infrastructure — license NASA's KSC smart corrosion-detecting coating, sell it as a tamper-evident corrosion *record* for Rio Grande Valley launch, pipeline, port and LNG assets | **8.57** |\n| 🥈 | Tamper-evident compliance evidence platform (FAA / TCEQ / PHMSA filings) | 7.03 |\n| 🥉 | Cryogenic boil-off recovery for Starbase and the Port of Brownsville | 6.59 |\n\nThe winner is a hybrid: a licensable NASA technology as the sensor, the evidence engine this repository already implements as the product.\n\nTwo results worth flagging because they cut against the obvious answer:\n\n- The **standalone evidence product was vetoed in round one** on regional economic impact, despite scoring 10/10 on founder advantage and capital efficiency. The rubric eliminated the applicant's own existing product rather than flattering it.\n- The verdict is **conditional on one unverified fact** (availability of the NASA KSC coating for license in 2026). If it fails, the runner-up wins. This is recorded as reversal condition `R-1` and is the first action in the submission plan.\n\n## Governance tier\n\n- [x] **Governance-lite**: documentation-only addition with no behavior, product-claim, acceptance-criterion, security, architecture, policy, courtroom, or schema change.\n- [ ] Governed: all other changes.\n\n**Why it qualifies:** every added path is under `docs/plan/expanding-frontiers-2026-08-28/`. No file under `src/`, `.autopilot/`, `.github/`, `evidence/`, or any schema is touched. The one added Python file (`score.py`) is a self-contained, dependency-free scorer for the documents in the same directory; it is not imported by the package and is outside `pyrightconfig.json`'s `include`. No product claim about Hive Mind OS is made or changed — the deliverable states explicitly that the repository is an early prototype and is not production-validated.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `dag_standard.py dag-lint --plan … --strict` | **0 error, 0 warning, 0 info** |\n| `dag_standard.py dag-rounds --plan … --expected-plan-digest …` | 8 rounds, exit 0, digest-bound |\n| `score.py` | Reproduces every weighted score and both veto outcomes from the published inputs |\n| `ruff check` on the added script | All checks passed |\n| `python -m compileall` on the added script | Passed |\n| `python -m unittest discover -s tests` | 1123 tests, 39 failures / 102 errors / 7 skipped |\n\n**On the test suite:** those failure counts are **pre-existing and unrelated to this change**. A clean clone checked out at `origin/main` was run separately and produced the identical result — 1123 tests, 39 failures, 102 errors, 7 skipped. This branch adds no code to `src/` or `tests/`, so it cannot affect them. They are reported here rather than omitted, but they are not this PR's to fix.\n\n**Reproducing the run:**\n\n```bash\npython .autopilot/bin/dag_standard.py --repo-root . dag-lint \\\n  --plan docs/plan/expanding-frontiers-2026-08-28/plan.json --strict\npython docs/plan/expanding-frontiers-2026-08-28/score.py\n```\n\n`RECEIPT.json` binds the plan digests, the three commands with their exit codes, and a SHA-256 digest of every artifact in the directory.\n\n## Safety\n\n- [x] No credentials, private data, or unrelated generated artifacts are included.\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\n**Evidence boundary, stated in the deliverable itself:** `expandingfrontiers.org` was blocked by this session's network egress proxy (`EGRESS_BLOCKED`). No sponsor fact was read from the organization's live site; all are cited to secondary sources (NASA, NSS, DOE, EDA, Rio Grande Valley press). Deadlines, prize amounts and eligibility rules are marked **unverified** and carried as blocking operator confirmations `C-1`…`C-5`. The `.hive-mind/autopilot-request.json` session state written by `autopilot run` is deliberately **not** committed, so the command stays runnable for the next subject.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01KxNCjAJVJLoJcApt5gitwn)_",
